--- !u!114 &2085566035
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2085566033}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e6f8ed6b62ee79e4197eb3c1ebcedb11, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  storyText: {fileID: 395069269}
  pagenumText: {fileID: 62415941}
  storyPages:
  - 'The trees stood motionless, their shadows cast across the clearing, forming
    a wall and a

    sense of security, and only the foliage swayed in the warm
    night breeze. Twilight descended

    on the forest, and with it came the fog,
    gently enveloping the space in a white haze. All the

    rustling and sounds
    only added to this atmosphere of calm and tranquility. The paths where

    rabbits
    had been hopping around during the day were now empty, peacefully covered by
    the

    fog. For the rabbits, it was a quiet time; a time of peace and safety.
    Most of the rabbits slept

    peacefully near their shelters, but some of the
    bravest ones who couldn''t sleep came out to

    hop around on the damp grass,
    breathe in the fresh night air, and stretch their paws.


    A tiny rabbit peeked
    out from behind a shelter and watched a female rabbit named Ash. She

    was
    hopping on two legs instead of four, heading closer to the clearing and further
    away

    from their shelters, where the moon could be seen through the fog.
    The rabbit followed her,

    timidly trying not to disturb her or get caught,
    hopping and sneaking through the nearby

    thickets and bushes.'
  - "Until she stopped and he froze, a second or two, and she turned her head sharply
    and\r\nlooked straight at the bush behind which he was hiding.\n\n\u201CI know
    you're there,\u201D said Ash\n\nThe little rabbit flinched and jumped out of
    the bushes, his ears drooping.\n\n\u201CI... I didn't mean to scare you or follow
    you,\u201D he muttered.\n\n\u201CThen why were you sneaking up on me, little
    one?\u201D she asked, looking closely at the\r\ncowering rabbit.\n\n\u201CI was
    curious why you had gone so far away and...\u201D he admitted, shifting from
    one paw to\r\nthe other. Looking at her paws, he looked away.\n"
  - "\nAsh noticed this but didn't give it any attention. She raised her head to
    the sky. Moonlight\r\nwas breaking through the gaps in the fog.\n\n\u201CThis
    is how I feel freedom, look how beautiful it is,\u201D said Ash.\n\nThe rabbit
    looked around, and in his eyes, the forest seemed to come alive: the grass\r\nsparkling
    under the moon, the fog, which was not so thick, resembled clouds above her,
    the\r\nfireflies that were like flickering flames, so bright and alive, and the
    plants illuminated by the\r\nmoonlight. Everything was so bright and beautiful.\n\n\u201CIt's...
    It's so...\u201D whispered the rabbit\n"
  - '

    And at that moment, Ash heard a crunch. With a jerk, the little rabbit''s
    head was torn from its

    body and disappeared into the fog, its body convulsing,
    its legs trembling slightly, falling

    lifeless onto the grass.


    Ash
    looked in shock at what was left of the rabbit''s body. In an instant, the body
    was

    dragged away by some kind of shadow into the depths of the fog. The
    next second, she

    heard the sounds of slaughter and a long howl, coming from
    the direction of the shelters

    where the other rabbits should have been at
    that moment.

    Ash forgets to be cautious and runs into the fog with all her
    might, running and running,

    jumping and hiding behind one bush and then
    another tree. Until she finally makes it home.'
  - "She thought that what had happened earlier was the most frightening moment of
    her life. But\r\nforget about that, what appeared before the rabbit's eyes pierced
    her with primal horror, a\r\nsticky fear ran down her spine, and she even pricked
    up her ears; in a small clearing\r\nsurrounded by trees and fog, a sea of blood
    lay before them, and the air smelled of iron,\r\nthen ammonia. All the smells
    mixed, and through the mist, she could just make out a snake\r\nswallowing a
    small rabbit whole, just two meters away from her. Ash was frightened, she\r\nquickly
    dove back into the bushes and began to sneak towards her family's house.\r\nBut
    then, right before her eyes, a fox appeared, and she recognized that large shadow.
    It\r\nwas tearing apart her fellow rabbit and devouring it right next to her.
    The rabbit froze in\r\nplace. \u201CWhat is going on here?\u201D she thought.
    \u201CSnakes and foxes hunting together, what the\r\nhell?\u201D Then her ears
    caught the sound of footsteps on the wet grass, which, for some\r\nreason, were
    too distinct, meaning the predator was close. The bush she was hiding behind\r\nmoved
    to the other side."
  - "Ash jumped back at the last moment, and right where she had been\r\njust a second
    ago, a wolf's jaws snapped menacingly. \u201CA wolf?\u201D The thought popped
    into her\r\nhead in a panic. She quickly began to back away, looking for a way
    to escape from the\r\npredator's reach. Then a growl came from its mouth:\n\n\u201CWhere
    are you going? Isn't it better to die with your kin and family?\u201D growled
    the wolf.\r\n\u201CWe're having so much fun.\u201D\n\n\u201CWe?\u201D she whispered.\n\n\u201CYes,
    this is our feast, we'll kill all the rabbits,\u201D growled the wolf. \u201CAnd
    you will be my sixth\r\ntreat. I've never eaten a rabbit standing on two legs
    before.\u201D"
  - 'And he pounced on her. At the last moment, Ash jumped back and ran as fast as
    she could,

    but she couldn''t see anything through the fog. She felt the
    blood on the ground sticking to

    her paws. She heard bloodcurdling screams
    from all around, the sounds of breaking bones

    and tearing flesh. Ash saw
    her mother''s face through the fog and how something of

    incredible size
    tore her to pieces. The rabbit ran on until she ran into the trunk of a large
    tree.

    At that moment, she scrambled with her last ounce of strength and
    jumped from branch to

    branch until she reached a large spreading branch.
    To her left, closer to the tree trunk, there

    was a hollow right in front
    of her. Climbing onto the branch, she finally gave herself three

    seconds
    to catch her breath, then slowly made her way to the hollow. If she slipped now,
    she

    would most likely fall to her death.'
  - "\u201CStep by step,\u201D Ash thought to herself. Below, there were loud cries,
    and suddenly she heard\r\nsomeone growling under the tree. She looked down and
    saw a silhouette that was clearly\r\nsomething...\r\nIt was definitely a bear.
    The rabbit rushed to the hollow, squeezed into it, pressed her ears to\r\nher
    head, and tried to be as quiet as possible, not making a sound.\n\nShe heard
    footsteps receding, and then again, someone's piercing scream; one of her fellow\r\nrabbits.
    For Ash, all this was a terrible shock. With every sound of carnage, she shivered
    to\r\nher bones, her paws clenched, and she tensed like a string with every squelching
    sound.\r\nAfter a while, the poor rabbit's body was so exhausted from the events
    that, simply feeling a\r\nlittle warmth in the hollow, despite her panic, her
    body shut down."
  - 'Dawn was breaking, the first rays of sunlight began to fall on the forest, dispelling
    the fog, a

    light morning breeze swayed the leaves of the tree crowns, and
    the wet grass covered with

    dew and blood began to shimmer in the sun that
    was breaking through the foliage.

    A new day dawned for all the inhabitants
    of the forest, except for the rabbits, who were

    attacked by hungry predators.


    Ash
    climbed down from the tree. She had taken two steps when her paw stumbled on

    bones.
    Looking up, she saw a small clearing, her home surrounded by trees. Their cozy

    rabbit
    home was destroyed, and bones and blood were everywhere. There was so much

    blood
    that it stuck to her little rabbit paws, and the smell of death was everywhere.'
  - "All the rabbits except her were dead. All her brothers and sisters, her family,
    her brother, and\r\nher mother had been eaten and torn to pieces by predators.
    Right before her eyes, the\r\nrabbits had been slaughtered and devoured whole.\n\nShe
    walked around the clearing and looked into every burrow, hoping to find someone.
    No\r\none. All that remained of them were bones and corpses scattered across
    the field, claw and\r\npaw marks of various sizes, and a bloody mess. \u201CAnd
    all because there was more than one\r\npredator,\u201D she thought, \u201CBut
    do predators hunt together, especially different predators?\u201D\n\n\u201CIt
    was planned,\u201D she whispered. \u201CWhy did they hunt together, for fun or
    for prey... for what?\n\nTears streamed from her small eyes. The place that had
    been her home was now a\r\ngraveyard. Nothing, no one. Why? WHY?"
  - "\u201CAh, but we are herbivores, predators should hunt us,\u201D an evil thought
    slipped into her head,\r\n\u201CWho said we have to be prey?\u201D Another thought
    crept into her head. She raised her head\r\nand, pricking up her ears, looked
    around the forest glade strewn with remains. Rage boiled\r\nup inside her with
    every passing second. \u201CI must take revenge!\u201D Suddenly, this thought\r\nflashed
    through her mind. She saw a skeleton lying a meter and a half away from her.
    She\r\nreflexively reached for it, picked it up in her paws, and dragged it toward
    a tree on the\r\nopposite side of the clearing, where there were stones. Ash
    first picked up a large stone and\r\nbegan to separate and crush the skeleton's
    bones. When she separated a sturdy bone, she\r\nbegan to sharpen it with the
    sharpest stone, making a dagger.\r\nAs she did so, her nature seemed to change,
    and there was only one word in her head:\r\nrevenge, revenge, revenge..."
  - 'The rabbit felt a rage and aggression rising from the depths, something she
    had never felt

    before, and everything around her became clearer and darker.
    The moment the dagger was

    ready, she looked at her companions once more,
    glanced at the dagger, and twirled it in her

    paw. And with a terrifying
    smile on her face, she said:'
  - "<color=red><b>\u201CI will take revenge on these bastards for you, let the hunt
    for the predators begin!\u201D</b>\t</color>"
